<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111664" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φί̄μ-ωσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>muzzling, silencing,</i> of death, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὶν φθάσαι τὴν φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Vett.Val.
					257.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>stopping up an orifice,</i> e.g. of the eye, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).812
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMed.Strassb.</u>
				p.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>contraction</i> of the prepuce, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				50.5.1
			</span></i>.</div>
